i6"],"evidence_ids":["mapping.long.record-257bm-i6"],"id":"long.record-257bm-i6","kind":"claim","label":"Long record Theorem 6.94 (An unconditional bound with one extra bit)","locator":"Long record Theorem 6.94, p. 71, label record:257bm-i6","source_id":"paper.long.pdf","statement":"*Unconditionally, for every $c\\ge4$ and every below-half core $D\\subseteq[2,c)$ with deficit $<\\ensuremath{w}(c)$:\n$$\n\\ensuremath{S}(D,1,2c-2) < 2^{c-1}.\n$$\nThe bound holds uniformly in $c$, but is twice the threshold needed in Theorem 6.93 to apply Theorem 6.75. Before using $|D|\\le c-2\\le2^{c-2}$, the proof gives the sharper additive estimate $\\ensuremath{S}(D,1,2c-2)<2^{c-2}+|D|$. Thus the critical-capacity inequality would follow by excluding the integer band $[2^{c-2},\\,2^{c-2}+c-3]$, which contains $c-2$ integers. This is the same band shape as Theorem 6.79’s dyadic-band condition. Its width is linear in $c$, whereas the square-root reset condition discussed in Section 12.5 has width $2^{(r+5)/2}$ in a different parameter $r$. Comparing these widths alone proves no implication between the two hypotheses.*","status":"unverified"},"ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i6","relations":[{"derived":false,"family":"arguments","from":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/nodes/long.record-257bm-i6","id":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i6%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_capacity_band_exclusion%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","kind":"formalizes","record_ref":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0cc1/edges/%5B%22long.record-257bm-i6%22%2C%22lean.ErdosProblems.Erdos257.PaperCompleteR21.paper_capacity_band_exclusion%22%2C%22formalizes%22%5D","semantic_class":"formalization_correspondence","to":"sha256:5d6514073ac52d75d011c84ff900912363a94ff7fe2e141210e6bf3c445c0c